{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK14TelemetryEventO","symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryEvent"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryEvent"}],"title":"TelemetryEvent"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryEvent","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"enum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rather than a protocol hierarchy, which is what makes §19.2 rule 3’s “no event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"payload may carry a secret” checkable rather than aspirational: the case list is closed, each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"case has a fixed associated-value list, and none of them is a dictionary. There is nowhere to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"put a token in a payload bound for a metrics backend — the type, not a review comment, is what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps them out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hooks are invoked on the calling task, so a sink must not block: §19.2 rule 4 makes buffering"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the caller’s job so they can pick the policy. Every mature metrics library already buffers."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/telemetryevent"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":